Condition: Moderate Diabetic Retinopathy

Dataset: EyePACS
Category: Diabetic retinopathy grade

General Information:
Moderate diabetic retinopathy represents progression beyond the mild stage. More retinal blood vessel abnormalities can develop as diabetes affects the small blood vessels supplying the retina.

Common Features:
Retinal photographs may show multiple microaneurysms, retinal hemorrhages, and other vascular changes. The exact findings vary between patients.

Common Causes and Risk Factors:
The condition is associated with diabetes and is influenced by factors such as duration of diabetes, blood glucose control, blood pressure, and other vascular risk factors.

General Management:
Management includes appropriate control of diabetes and cardiovascular risk factors together with regular eye examinations. Further ophthalmic evaluation may be needed depending on retinal findings.

RAG Safety Note:
This information is for general educational context in the MedVision prototype. It should not be used alone to diagnose or treat a patient.

Source/Verification Note:
Medical information should be verified against current authoritative clinical references before use in a clinical setting.
